WEBVTT

00:06.650 --> 00:08.480
Good morning!

00:08.650 --> 00:10.860
It's past noon! And you're finally awake!

00:10.940 --> 00:13.070
You just moved in
and you're already being shameless.

00:13.070 --> 00:15.990
I'm a vampire so that makes me
a night owl.

00:15.990 --> 00:19.120
In the morning my eyes are droopy,
but at night, they're glaring.

00:19.120 --> 00:21.370
It's like you're not suited
for communal living.

00:21.580 --> 00:25.710
Oh, Morihito, can I please get
one of those? If you know what I mean.

00:25.710 --> 00:27.250
That's a weird way to ask.

00:29.420 --> 00:31.130
<i>The vampire Miharu Kiryu,</i>

00:31.130 --> 00:34.800
<i>along with eating meals,
needs to use Drain to siphon life energy.</i>

00:35.970 --> 00:39.310
Oh man, Morihito's energy first thing
in the morning is just the greatest.

00:39.310 --> 00:41.310
Did Miharu just get high off Morihito?

00:41.310 --> 00:42.930
What am I watching?

00:43.230 --> 00:45.480
What does it feel like for you, Moi?

00:46.270 --> 00:50.270
Miharu's father got all wrinkly because
he got Drained for five years.

00:50.270 --> 00:53.190
Don't say "wrinkly." I feel fine.

00:53.740 --> 00:56.200
An ogre's life energy
has the best volume and quality.

00:56.360 --> 00:58.870
And the purity level is off the charts.

00:58.870 --> 00:59.950
Please stop.

00:59.950 --> 01:01.910
Then here, Miharu.
Try siphoning mine.

01:01.910 --> 01:04.830
Oh, tengu energy is a little...
No thank you.

01:04.830 --> 01:07.290
- Wait, what?
- I'm really sorry!

01:07.290 --> 01:09.290
Why're you being so cheeky
with your tongue?

01:11.000 --> 01:13.260
Go ahead and try me, too.

01:13.260 --> 01:14.050
What?

01:14.220 --> 01:17.640
I've got tons of magic power,
so go ahead.

01:17.640 --> 01:19.510
Oh, hey!

01:21.350 --> 01:22.810
Nico!

01:22.810 --> 01:24.390
Nico, are you okay?

01:25.270 --> 01:29.980
I'm not siphoning magic power,
so even if you have lots of it,

01:29.980 --> 01:32.320
you still have the same amount
of life energy as a normal girl.

01:32.440 --> 01:35.360
I wanted to help in some way.

01:35.360 --> 01:37.700
That's dangerous,
so don't be so reckless.

01:37.820 --> 01:42.580
However, Drain also siphons a small
amount of the person's feelings.

01:42.580 --> 01:45.450
And I felt your warm friendship, Nico.

01:48.330 --> 01:52.210
Admiration and gratitude.
Innocent and wonderful.

01:52.420 --> 01:54.840
All with a slight tinge of bittersweet...

01:55.210 --> 01:57.590
from your love for Morihito.

02:07.560 --> 02:09.480
Sorry, I couldn't hear anything.

02:09.480 --> 02:13.570
I was testing my noise canceling
ear buds that I just bought.

02:16.280 --> 02:18.610
<i>Miharu has joined our group!</i>

03:49.200 --> 03:51.250
Why did you say that? Are you an idiot?

03:51.580 --> 03:53.670
I thought my heart was gonna stop.

03:51.830 --> 03:56.630
MIHARU KIRYU, THE VAMPIRE

03:53.670 --> 03:56.210
Oh, I wasn't supposed to say that, was I?

03:56.210 --> 03:59.210
Stop blurting out anything
that comes to mind.

03:59.210 --> 04:03.130
I'm sorry, I wanted
to get along with everyone,

04:03.800 --> 04:06.390
so I got nervous and went too far.

04:06.640 --> 04:08.260
I'm terribly sorry.

04:10.470 --> 04:15.650
I'm an only child, so it feels like I suddenly
got an older sister and brothers.

04:15.650 --> 04:18.520
It made me happy and I got excited.

04:18.520 --> 04:19.690
Urgh!

04:20.320 --> 04:23.200
You're doing this because
you know you're cute.

04:23.360 --> 04:26.410
I also want to hang out
with each of you guys, too.

04:26.410 --> 04:28.030
Keigo, I'd like to go
watch movies with you.

04:28.030 --> 04:28.950
Urgh!

04:28.950 --> 04:31.370
Nico, I'd like to visit sweets cafés
and eat lots of anmitsu.

04:31.370 --> 04:32.290
Urgh!

04:32.290 --> 04:34.210
Kanshi, I'd like to play
gacha games with you.

04:34.420 --> 04:36.130
Urgh!

04:36.130 --> 04:37.710
Wait, stop making us go, "Urgh!"

04:37.710 --> 04:40.210
Oh, by the way, where's Morihito?

04:40.210 --> 04:41.590
He went shopping.

04:41.800 --> 04:44.430
That's right, Morihito asked me

04:44.430 --> 04:49.050
to teach you the rules of the house today,
as your senpai.

04:49.470 --> 04:51.100
Okay! Take it away, Senpai!

04:51.100 --> 04:52.140
I'm over here!

04:52.140 --> 04:55.560
Oh, I just thought saying,
"as your senpai" was kind of a lot, so...

04:55.560 --> 04:56.650
What?

04:56.650 --> 05:01.230
I was getting power harassment vibes,
so is it okay if I record this conversation?

05:01.230 --> 05:02.440
Urgh!

05:02.650 --> 05:05.450
He's easily making us go, "Urgh."

05:06.530 --> 05:11.200
Listen up! The most important part about
communal living is splitting up the chores.

05:11.490 --> 05:15.540
You probably got spoiled by your parents
and had them do everything,

05:15.540 --> 05:18.330
but that won't cut it here, newbie!

05:18.330 --> 05:22.670
Saying things in a way to assert
dominance from the get-go is so cringe.

05:22.840 --> 05:24.800
So how're the chores split up so far?

05:24.800 --> 05:27.590
I'm in charge of cleaning
the first floor's bathroom.

05:27.800 --> 05:29.600
I take care of the second floor bathroom.

05:29.600 --> 05:31.100
And I do the second floor bathtub.

05:33.680 --> 05:35.060
That's it?

05:35.060 --> 05:36.980
Wait, what? Then who cooks?

05:36.980 --> 05:38.100
Morihito.

05:38.100 --> 05:39.270
And the cleanup?

05:39.270 --> 05:40.270
Morihito.

05:40.270 --> 05:41.440
Who cleans the house?

05:41.440 --> 05:42.480
Also Moi.

05:42.820 --> 05:44.280
He kinda just does it for us.

05:44.280 --> 05:46.240
You guys are being spoiled rotten!

05:46.400 --> 05:47.820
Wait, you don't understand.

05:47.820 --> 05:50.780
In the past, we did take turns
doing the cooking and cleaning,

05:50.780 --> 05:53.660
but there was fire, things burned and broke,
and it turned into a nightmare.

05:53.660 --> 05:55.540
So he said,
"Never mind, I'll just do it."

05:55.540 --> 05:58.500
I understand everything!
That's what "being spoiled" means!

05:58.710 --> 06:00.920
However, we all do our own laundry.

06:00.920 --> 06:03.340
Well, yeah, I wouldn't want
to wash your underwear, either!

06:03.340 --> 06:04.960
Stop trying to be a poser about it.

06:05.170 --> 06:07.420
I think I'm starting to get it.

06:07.800 --> 06:11.970
Morihito has a strong sense of responsibility,
and is serious and certain about cleanliness.

06:11.970 --> 06:13.640
You guys are just klutzes.

06:13.640 --> 06:14.600
So brutal.

06:15.600 --> 06:17.600
But it's just as you say.

06:17.810 --> 06:20.190
If it weren't for Moi,
I'd probably be in a gross room

06:20.190 --> 06:23.230
eating convenience store food
and having fruit fly problems!

06:23.480 --> 06:27.070
I do feel bad, you know.
I feel bad all the time!

06:27.320 --> 06:30.780
For a long time,
I couldn't come to like myself,

06:31.030 --> 06:33.330
and it's like I finally found
a place where I belong? But like...

06:33.450 --> 06:35.620
They've started mumbling something.

06:35.620 --> 06:38.580
This household has become
completely reliant on Morihito.

06:38.790 --> 06:42.000
All right, then. We have to do this!

06:42.670 --> 06:47.920
Let's all prepare a meal together and
surprise Morihito so hard that he cries!

06:50.630 --> 06:52.510
Heck yeah!

06:52.890 --> 06:55.180
Let's make Morihito cry.

06:55.180 --> 06:58.310
Miharu, you're such a good kid.
Thank you so much.

06:58.310 --> 07:01.980
Damn it, they're already so emotionally
touched that they've started crying.

07:02.900 --> 07:04.230
I'm home.

07:04.400 --> 07:06.030
Sorry I took so long.

07:09.150 --> 07:11.990
There's fire, things are burning
and broken!

07:12.360 --> 07:13.990
It's a nightmare in here!

07:15.450 --> 07:17.240
Tell me what happened here!

07:17.660 --> 07:22.120
I wanted to band everyone together...
and make a meal for you.

07:22.580 --> 07:25.340
However, I chopped my finger
when I was using the knife.

07:25.340 --> 07:26.750
Please be careful.

07:26.750 --> 07:30.760
I panicked and tried to heal myself,
so I Drained Keigo, but then he fainted.

07:30.760 --> 07:32.760
Dayside has
a normal amount of life energy!

07:32.970 --> 07:36.760
That's when Nico panicked and splashed
water onto the tempura oil,

07:36.760 --> 07:38.270
which created a fire pillar.

07:38.560 --> 07:41.060
That's when Kanshi panicked
and tried to blow the fire out,

07:41.060 --> 07:43.020
but he created a flamethrower instead.

07:43.650 --> 07:45.270
That's when I got some bad burns.

07:45.270 --> 07:47.440
It's like a Pythagora Switch episode
from hell.

07:47.860 --> 07:50.150
Then when Nico saw me, she fainted, too.

07:50.320 --> 07:52.740
Kanshi is concentrating on putting out the fire,

07:52.740 --> 07:55.740
and I'm on the verge of death
because of blood loss and these burns.

07:55.740 --> 07:57.790
A-All right, I understand.

07:58.740 --> 08:00.040
I'm sorry.

08:00.160 --> 08:01.790
It's all my fault.

08:02.040 --> 08:05.380
I wanted to ease your burden,
and brought up the idea.

08:05.540 --> 08:06.840
I take full responsibility!

08:06.840 --> 08:09.420
I wanted to do good, so please blame me,
the person who took charge!

08:09.590 --> 08:12.510
Don't you dare try to look good!
You're just a klutz, too!

08:12.510 --> 08:13.550
It's all right.

08:13.840 --> 08:16.050
I was worried about you, Miharu.

08:16.350 --> 08:18.010
This house is full of quirky people,

08:18.010 --> 08:20.680
but it looks like you're getting
used to things, so I'm glad.

08:23.440 --> 08:25.810
I'm glad, too.

08:26.110 --> 08:28.690
I ended up Draining everyone here,

08:28.690 --> 08:31.820
and was able to touch upon
the feelings that came flowing in.

08:32.320 --> 08:36.120
Everyone shared the feeling
that living here is really fun.

08:44.080 --> 08:45.290
Urgh.

08:48.840 --> 08:50.630
You lost my parasol?

08:51.130 --> 08:52.590
Yeah, I'm really sorry.

08:51.130 --> 08:56.930
MISSING PARASOL

08:52.590 --> 08:55.130
I just borrowed it,
but it got pilfered while I was out.

08:55.260 --> 08:58.350
What? You just took my parasol,
the second most important thing to me,

08:58.350 --> 08:59.760
without even asking?

08:59.850 --> 09:02.980
Please die to make up for it.
I'll provide the blade.

09:02.980 --> 09:05.480
I said I'm sorry! But listen, okay?

09:05.480 --> 09:08.270
It's not like it got stolen because
I wasn't being careful. Hear me out.

09:08.520 --> 09:11.650
This morning, I wanted to go to
the convenience store, but it was raining.

09:11.650 --> 09:14.740
And then, on my way home,
a man asked me for directions.

09:14.740 --> 09:18.530
He even asked me to draw a map,
so I had him hold the parasol.

09:19.990 --> 09:21.330
When I looked up, he was gone.

09:21.330 --> 09:23.370
You were definitely
not being careful at all!

09:23.950 --> 09:27.040
It sounds like you just made up
that story, too. You're definitely lying!

09:27.170 --> 09:28.880
I-I'm not lying!

09:28.880 --> 09:31.090
H-He was wearing sunglasses,
had a cloth over his head,

09:31.090 --> 09:33.960
a burglar's mustache,
and a sack with karakusa swirls.

09:33.960 --> 09:36.010
This tengu sure lies a lot!

09:36.010 --> 09:38.260
What kind of character
did you just make up?

09:38.260 --> 09:41.220
Even if you fabricate such a story,
your punishment won't get lighter!

09:41.810 --> 09:43.310
This isn't good.

09:43.600 --> 09:46.850
Miharu has a condition where
he can't last five minutes in direct sunlight.

09:46.850 --> 09:48.810
Parasols are a requirement
during summer.

09:48.900 --> 09:51.270
Plus it was custom-made
with a hidden sword.

09:51.270 --> 09:54.150
All right, I get it!
I'll go back out and look for it.

09:54.150 --> 09:58.320
It's fine! I'll just go out
and buy a replacement parasol.

09:58.950 --> 10:01.950
I do not want to hold something
unless it's beautiful.

10:01.950 --> 10:03.580
I understand, Miharu.

10:01.950 --> 10:03.580
PEOPLE WITH A SENSE OF TASTE

10:03.910 --> 10:06.960
Picky people are so troublesome.

10:07.620 --> 10:11.090
I'm taking an umbrella to use as a parasol.

10:11.090 --> 10:13.300
Ugh, why did it have to be me?

10:13.300 --> 10:16.130
Oh, I have a good spell for you.

10:16.130 --> 10:16.920
What?

10:16.920 --> 10:18.930
Cloud Crown!

10:20.140 --> 10:21.850
And I'm off!

10:23.140 --> 10:24.390
There he goes.

10:24.390 --> 10:26.600
Will he really be okay with that?

10:27.060 --> 10:28.060
He should be.

10:38.570 --> 10:40.870
<i>Cloud Crown!</i>

10:43.330 --> 10:45.370
Whoa! There's a cloud above my head!

10:45.620 --> 10:47.910
It's a spell that reflects
how you're feeling inside.

10:47.910 --> 10:51.290
Your heart is feeling gloomy,
so it's cloudy right now.

10:51.290 --> 10:53.250
Now you can avoid the sunlight.

10:53.250 --> 10:55.630
A mysterious spell that I don't
understand the original purpose of...

10:56.010 --> 10:59.510
But this should work. Thank you, Nico!

10:59.630 --> 11:01.760
Oh no, you can't feel happy!

11:02.340 --> 11:03.800
Because the clouds will go away.

11:03.800 --> 11:06.520
So does this mean
I have to feel gloomy all the time?

11:06.520 --> 11:10.730
A DOG OF FLANDERS

11:06.930 --> 11:10.730
Oh Patrasche, my poor Patrasche.

11:10.940 --> 11:13.110
Let us lie down and die together.

11:13.110 --> 11:16.360
Men have no need for us,
and we are all alone.

11:16.360 --> 11:18.280
Let us lie down and die.

11:18.570 --> 11:23.530
Ugh, why do I have to feel so sad
while going out to buy a parasol?

11:23.950 --> 11:26.580
Anyway, I have to maintain
these dark feelings.

11:26.580 --> 11:30.410
If I have fun or have happy feelings,
it'll cost me my life.

11:32.000 --> 11:33.290
Hello!

11:33.500 --> 11:35.880
Wow, such a pretty person.

11:35.880 --> 11:37.590
They're a foreigner.

11:37.590 --> 11:39.630
They've got a cloud, too.

11:39.920 --> 11:44.090
Oh, I know about this.
They're called angels!

11:48.850 --> 11:52.650
Dang it! My feelings were purified
around such innocence!

11:52.650 --> 11:54.730
I have to feel miserable again!

11:55.110 --> 11:59.190
Let's see, the anxiety of an obscure future,
I broke my smartphone screen,

11:59.190 --> 12:01.400
the guy next to me was speaking
too casually to the staff,

12:01.400 --> 12:03.110
a tengu who makes excuses and lies,

12:03.110 --> 12:06.580
my bike seat got stolen
and there was broccoli there.

12:10.370 --> 12:12.080
Will you marry me?

12:12.330 --> 12:14.210
Oh no! It's a heartwarming scene!

12:16.540 --> 12:17.670
Come on, don't...

12:17.670 --> 12:19.340
Don't laugh!

12:19.340 --> 12:21.010
Hi, we're comedians.

12:21.010 --> 12:23.340
If it's all right, can you listen
to our performance?

12:23.340 --> 12:25.050
<i>They're just trying
to kick away the cloud.</i>

12:25.050 --> 12:27.100
Hey there,
we're the Cloud-Kickin' Fog-Punchers.

12:27.100 --> 12:28.220
<i>Even the name!</i>

12:28.430 --> 12:32.690
We're actually a very unique
kind of fashion model.

12:32.690 --> 12:36.310
Don't beat around the bush,
we're just ugly and tall-fat.

12:36.310 --> 12:39.480
Despite what I look like on the outside,
I'm beautiful on the inside.

12:39.780 --> 12:43.110
The other day, I wanted to show off my
birthday suit, but when I arrived at the mixer,

12:43.110 --> 12:44.860
they kicked me out.

12:44.860 --> 12:47.620
Why would you go there naked though?

12:48.950 --> 12:50.120
<i>Oh thank god.</i>

12:50.330 --> 12:52.250
Thanks for listening.

12:52.250 --> 12:55.040
Huh? Is there snow falling on you?

12:55.040 --> 12:58.380
Please keep going with your work.
I like it when people challenge themselves.

12:58.500 --> 13:01.090
That's really encouraging to hear that.

13:01.090 --> 13:05.680
Especially after being made fun of
and being told that we look creepy.

13:06.180 --> 13:08.850
Well, one more thing to laugh about.

13:09.100 --> 13:11.770
You should just punch people like that.

13:13.520 --> 13:16.810
You turned a characteristic that
you were born with into a weapon.

13:16.810 --> 13:18.230
I think that's beautiful.

13:25.360 --> 13:27.910
<i>Why do I need a parasol?</i>

13:28.200 --> 13:31.580
<i>Because you were born with something
that makes you different from the others.</i>

13:43.380 --> 13:44.170
Huh?

13:47.550 --> 13:50.050
Is that my parasol?

13:53.430 --> 13:54.350
Hey.

13:58.690 --> 14:02.190
Give me back that parasol.
You stole it, didn't you?

14:02.320 --> 14:04.690
What? Who's this kid?

14:05.860 --> 14:06.950
Sunglasses,

14:07.280 --> 14:08.200
cloth on his head,

14:08.490 --> 14:09.450
a burglar's mustache,

14:09.700 --> 14:11.450
and a sack with karakusa swirls!

14:11.740 --> 14:14.330
So Kanshi wasn't lying after all?

14:14.540 --> 14:18.580
Huh? Do you have some kinda proof
that I stole it?

14:18.920 --> 14:21.000
Let's see it, then!

14:21.000 --> 14:22.800
Or you're gonna eat spaghetti
with your nose!

14:22.800 --> 14:24.090
The way he talks is trash, too!

14:24.090 --> 14:28.340
Your creepy blond hair reminds me
of that super boring comedian duo!

14:28.340 --> 14:30.510
And he was that awful person
who dissed the comedians!

14:30.800 --> 14:33.510
It all makes sense!

14:35.470 --> 14:37.890
Since my suspicions came to light,
the clouds also went away.

14:39.810 --> 14:45.030
No good, slowly fading out...
so I can't take hold of my feelings...

14:45.440 --> 14:48.280
Damn it all, so close...

14:48.610 --> 14:50.280
If I could just...

15:03.130 --> 15:04.800
Bird-Blackened Sky.

15:05.000 --> 15:05.920
Kanshi!

15:07.130 --> 15:08.220
I'll let you have this one.

15:08.220 --> 15:09.590
What the hell...

15:21.730 --> 15:24.060
I love black after all.

15:24.570 --> 15:26.230
It blocks the sunlight.

15:27.820 --> 15:28.990
And it's so beautiful.

15:32.360 --> 15:35.910
So that suspicious story was true, huh?

15:35.910 --> 15:37.750
I was trying to tell you!

15:37.750 --> 15:40.750
Well, it was my fault
that your parasol got stolen.

15:43.830 --> 15:46.500
Shall we both apologize
on "one, two, three, go"?

15:46.670 --> 15:48.760
Yeah, let's do that.

15:50.590 --> 15:52.180
One, two, three, and go!

15:52.180 --> 15:53.260
I'm sor...

15:53.890 --> 15:57.640
- Hey come on, you gotta say it, too!
- You fell for it!

16:06.480 --> 16:08.280
What? They're not here?

16:08.480 --> 16:12.240
Nico said you were coming,
so she went out to get some stuff.

16:08.860 --> 16:14.030
I'M SO GLAD YOU'RE HERE

16:12.240 --> 16:16.700
I'm sure she'll be home soon.
Morihito also went out to buy something.

16:15.160 --> 16:18.290
CAN I COME OVER TOMORROW?

16:15.780 --> 16:18.290
OF COURSE!

16:15.780 --> 16:18.540
<i>It's because I made a promise
that I'm not used to.</i>

16:16.700 --> 16:18.540
Kanshi and Miharu
also have something going on.

16:18.740 --> 16:21.080
<i>So I arrived way too early.</i>

16:21.410 --> 16:23.460
Then I'll come back later.

16:23.670 --> 16:24.540
Wait.

16:26.750 --> 16:28.210
<i>So awkward.</i>

16:28.630 --> 16:30.550
<i>Today's real goal...</i>

16:30.710 --> 16:34.800
<i>is to show Keigo a crescent shape
so he can change into Wolf.</i>

16:35.260 --> 16:37.640
<i>Come visit once a month.</i>

16:38.220 --> 16:39.970
<i>The difficult part is that</i>

16:39.970 --> 16:44.310
<i>I have to make it seem like it happened
naturally so he doesn't remember it.</i>

16:44.560 --> 16:47.020
<i>Such a strange mission I'm on.</i>

16:47.230 --> 16:50.570
<i>Anyway, I was told to wait inside.</i>

16:50.820 --> 16:54.570
<i>But what's with him?
He doesn't talk at all.</i>

16:54.740 --> 16:56.990
<i>Do you have a job
where you inspect curtains?</i>

16:57.070 --> 16:58.830
<i>Or are you someone
who can't talk to girls?</i>

16:59.370 --> 17:02.620
<i>Then it'll be such a quiet world
since I can't talk to boys.</i>

17:02.750 --> 17:05.830
<i>I really just want to slam a croissant
in his face and go home.</i>

17:06.130 --> 17:08.960
<i>I mean, we don't really have a shared
interest that we can talk about.</i>

17:09.090 --> 17:12.510
<i>I wonder if there are any
conversation starters around here.</i>

17:13.920 --> 17:14.800
Hey.

17:15.180 --> 17:16.800
Can we go to your room?

17:16.800 --> 17:17.890
What?

17:20.470 --> 17:22.600
<i>I said something really drastic.</i>

17:22.930 --> 17:26.350
<i>Now that I think about it, saying that
I want to go to a boy's room</i>

17:26.520 --> 17:27.860
<i>was a bad idea, wasn't it?</i>

17:28.150 --> 17:30.480
<i>I wonder if he thought
I was some shameless woman.</i>

17:32.360 --> 17:35.820
<i>This girl is really, really pretty.</i>

17:36.320 --> 17:39.740
<i>How am I supposed to look her
in the face and talk to her?</i>

17:39.910 --> 17:42.370
<i>B-But she came out all this way,</i>

17:42.370 --> 17:45.000
<i>so I have to say something
so she doesn't get bored.</i>

17:45.120 --> 17:46.370
Oh, hey.

17:47.210 --> 17:48.920
Have you checked out the sky recently?

17:48.920 --> 17:49.790
Excuse me?

17:51.500 --> 17:54.760
I realized that I haven't looked at it lately,

17:54.760 --> 17:57.430
so yesterday, I laid down on a bench
and looked at the clouds all day.

17:57.430 --> 17:59.760
<i>Oh gosh, he's being such a poser.</i>

18:00.050 --> 18:03.770
<i>What should I do?
It's such a despairingly boring topic.</i>

18:04.140 --> 18:07.350
<i>Ugh, let's just do what I came here
to do so I can go home.</i>

18:08.020 --> 18:10.860
<i>"The Sky is So Unlimitedly Sky Blue."</i>

18:10.980 --> 18:14.240
<i>This movie has a scene
where the crescent moon comes out.</i>

18:14.360 --> 18:16.530
<i>It's the first arrow
for the "Crescent Strategy."</i>

18:16.740 --> 18:17.660
Hey!

18:18.160 --> 18:19.780
Would you like to watch a movie together?

18:19.780 --> 18:21.780
A-A movie? With me?

18:21.910 --> 18:25.540
That's right. I even brought some cake,
so let's have some while we watch.

18:25.960 --> 18:29.380
<i>Wow. It's just us now.</i>

18:29.540 --> 18:31.540
<i>We've come to this park before, right?</i>

18:31.750 --> 18:35.550
<i>This situation is like a girlfriend
who came to visit her boyfriend's house.</i>

18:35.630 --> 18:37.630
<i>Did I get the situation wrong?</i>

18:38.800 --> 18:42.010
<i>When the movie started,
he got really quiet and focused.</i>

18:42.010 --> 18:44.100
<i>Come on, eat some of the cake, too.</i>

18:45.350 --> 18:48.310
<i>They're hiding behind his scraggly hair,
but if you look closely,</i>

18:48.310 --> 18:50.690
<i>he has big eyes,
a prominent nose bridge,</i>

18:50.690 --> 18:53.940
<i>and he has a delicate facial
structure but a manly chin.</i>

18:55.190 --> 18:56.690
<i>But anyway...</i>

18:56.690 --> 18:58.860
<i>It's taking a while to get
to that crescent moon scene.</i>

18:58.860 --> 19:00.700
<i>This silence is so unbearable!</i>

19:00.700 --> 19:02.530
<i>He'll think that I'm nervous
or something.</i>

19:02.530 --> 19:04.450
<i>If we could just talk about something...</i>

19:04.450 --> 19:06.290
<i>So, what kinds of things
are you good at?</i>

19:06.290 --> 19:07.160
<i>Let's see...</i>

19:07.160 --> 19:08.460
Oh, that's right.

19:08.460 --> 19:10.210
Huh? What?

19:10.670 --> 19:12.840
What kind of magic do you specialize in?

19:13.670 --> 19:16.090
I've never seen you cast any spells.

19:16.300 --> 19:18.130
Oh, I just have really normal spells.

19:18.130 --> 19:20.590
I can only use basic spells and such.

19:20.760 --> 19:23.300
<i>I still don't want my shapeshifting
magic to get exposed!</i>

19:23.300 --> 19:25.850
I heard you were from
an elite witch family, so...

19:28.310 --> 19:31.100
Yes, my mother is a brilliant witch.

19:31.480 --> 19:34.690
And I do eventually
need to become like her.

19:34.690 --> 19:36.610
But I'm pretty average.

19:36.940 --> 19:42.110
My mother is disappointed in me,
because I'm not talented like Nico.

19:43.030 --> 19:45.780
I wish I wasn't born into a witch family.

19:45.950 --> 19:48.620
I think a normal lifestyle
would've suited me more.

19:48.950 --> 19:51.120
I'd like to complain to God if I could.

19:52.120 --> 19:53.880
<i>It's not your fault!</i>

19:54.080 --> 19:56.000
<i>It's the world that is to blame!</i>

19:57.340 --> 19:58.960
Why did you turn it off?

19:58.960 --> 20:00.470
It's a boring movie.

20:01.510 --> 20:06.390
And if that God said they could turn you
into a normal human, would you do it?

20:11.230 --> 20:12.520
I wouldn't.

20:14.360 --> 20:16.860
Bad things might've happened,

20:16.860 --> 20:18.980
but I'm sure there were
some good memories, too.

20:18.980 --> 20:21.450
Memories that are important to you.

20:22.360 --> 20:24.410
And I'm a werewolf, you know?

20:24.780 --> 20:27.790
There are lots of things
you can't change when you're born.

20:27.790 --> 20:30.200
So it won't really help
if you just complain about it.

20:30.200 --> 20:33.040
If you start blaming other people,
you won't be able to stop.

20:33.420 --> 20:36.670
I get pissed at Wolf,
but I won't complain.

20:36.920 --> 20:40.800
And that's because, since I'm a werewolf,
I was able to meet everyone.

20:46.140 --> 20:49.180
You finally talked to me
without trying to be cool.

20:49.810 --> 20:51.600
Oh no, I didn't mean to...

20:52.430 --> 20:54.850
This cake is delicious.
Wait, did you get upset?

20:54.850 --> 20:57.440
I did get upset
at how you turned off the movie.

20:57.570 --> 20:59.530
I-I'm so sorry, let's keep watching.

20:59.530 --> 21:00.940
No, that's okay.

21:01.610 --> 21:04.030
<i>Because the second arrow is about to hit.</i>

21:09.490 --> 21:11.540
You did well, Nemu Miyao!

21:11.540 --> 21:12.870
All right, I shall head home.

21:12.870 --> 21:13.830
Wait!

21:14.000 --> 21:16.540
I'm gonna go outside,
so you stay here in the house!

21:16.540 --> 21:20.590
Why me? If you're too reckless,
Morihito will scold you!

21:21.550 --> 21:24.220
Then, wanna spend some time
with me here?

21:26.760 --> 21:29.560
That's right, you guys
were having a fun conversation.

21:29.560 --> 21:32.730
Keigo said he was happy
that he met everyone.

21:32.930 --> 21:35.730
What about you, Nemu Miyao?

21:36.940 --> 21:39.060
N-No, I'm not...

21:39.060 --> 21:40.480
We're home!

21:41.690 --> 21:43.360
I'm so glad you're here!

21:43.690 --> 21:46.530
Nemu? You sure got here early.

21:46.530 --> 21:48.530
I'm sorry to make you wait.

21:49.280 --> 21:51.120
Hey! You've turned into Wolf!

21:51.450 --> 21:52.910
What did you do to Nemu?

21:52.910 --> 21:54.500
I haven't done anything, yet.

21:54.500 --> 21:55.790
Yet?!

21:56.040 --> 22:00.960
<i>You were a lot cooler when you weren't
trying to be cool, Keigo Magami.</i>

23:33.760 --> 23:35.600
Moi, what's this?

23:35.600 --> 23:39.060
I went out to Hands to buy some materials
so I could make these.

23:39.770 --> 23:40.810
It's a doorplate.

23:46.650 --> 23:48.740
<i>And so, lots of things have happened,</i>

23:48.740 --> 23:53.530
<i>but an ogre, a witch, a vampire,
a tengu, and a werewolf...</i>

23:54.160 --> 23:55.990
<i>are all having a great time living together!</i>

23:58.040 --> 24:00.710
The doorplate that Moi made is so cute!

24:00.710 --> 24:02.670
I like how there's
a marking and number on it.

24:02.670 --> 24:05.040
This item definitely screams merchandise.

24:05.040 --> 24:07.050
The welcome cookies were cute, too.

24:05.960 --> 24:12.050
NEXT EPISODE
WE GOT TRAPPED IN A DEATH GAME...
LONG LONG A GO GO

24:07.050 --> 24:09.760
If there's a collaboration café,
it should definitely be on the menu.

24:09.760 --> 24:11.680
All right, stop talking about it already!
